+### OWASP review
+
+| Category | Risk | Required mitigation/test |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| A01 Broken access control | Cross-tenant session/slice discovery or worker forgery. | Server-derived scope; tenant-composite keys/FKs; current-membership check; uniform denial; least-privilege role negatives. |
+| A02 Cryptographic failures | Digest treated as authenticity or secrets/raw URLs logged. | SHA-256 is content identity only; TLS/provider encryption remain required; no presigned URLs/secrets/content in DB logs or errors. |
+| A03 Injection | Dynamic status/range/worker SQL. | Parameterized SQL, fixed enum/state vocabulary, bounded numeric validation, no identifier interpolation. |
+| A04 Insecure design | ACK before durable object/transaction; deletion races processing. | Explicit transaction/state machines, leases, crash tests, fail-closed unknown outcome. |
+| A05 Misconfiguration | Owner role or production project used in tests. | Existing authority validator; disposable test project/root; runtime privilege negatives; required cleanup. |
+| A07 Auth failures | Stale/replayed actor or consent. | Revalidate current membership/meeting access; immutable policy-bound consent; no client scope fields. |
+| A08 Integrity failures | Same sequence overwritten with different bytes; duplicate transcript. | Conditional content-addressed write, digest mismatch rejection, unique relational output keys. |
+| A09 Logging failures | Missing recovery evidence or sensitive observability. | Structured opaque IDs/state/codes/attempts; no audio/transcript/URL/token; exact-head artifacts. |
+| A10 SSRF | Persisted arbitrary object URL opened by worker. | Store provider/bucket/key only; adapter builds endpoint from trusted config; reject URLs from payload/DB. |
