+## Rollout and rollback
+
+- Each PR is sequential, independently reversible, and capped at 300 hand-authored production lines. If a slice exceeds the cap, split before review; do not hide behavior in generated files.
+- Schema is additive. Application rollback leaves unused capture tables/columns in place; it never runs a down migration, edits Drizzle history, or deletes acknowledged raw objects.
+- Before any production migration, a human-approved release records exact main SHA, migration tag/hash/floor, project/branch/database, restore point/branch, row counts, role grants, and pending exact suffix. This PLAN does not perform it.
+- A pre-traffic failure permits an application-only revert. Once any capture session exists, rollback must remain ledger-compatible: never run a down migration, rewrite history, delete acknowledged objects, or restore over rows automatically. A Neon restore is a separate human data-loss decision from a verified restore point/branch.
+- After any session exists, the capability gate disables only **new session creation** until recovery closes; existing sessions, slice retries, status, finalize, STT recovery, and deletion continue through the approved recovery window. No rollback may strand a pending ACK/work row.
